<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span><span id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CARVE</span> Implementations.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Representation Construction.</span> We split each video into non-overlapping <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="120" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>120</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">120</annotation></semantics></math>-second segments and build four representations per segment, indexed identically across representations. The VF encodes <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> keyframes per segment; the VC encodes up to <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math> frames per segment (maximum <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}843{,}200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,843,200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}843{,}200</annotation></semantics></math> pixels per frame, sampled at <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> fps). The TF view captions the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math> keyframes with Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> up to <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> tokens; the TC view captions per-second frames at <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> fps.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Retrieval and Generation.</h4>

<div id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At inference, we retrieve the top-<math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}5</annotation></semantics></math> chunks per query, with reranking using the default Qwen3-VL-Reranker-2B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. The retrieved chunks are passed to Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct with a maximum of <math id="A4.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> new tokens under its default decoding setup. Every generated answer is judged against the reference by a binary judge (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B), using identical judge weights and prompt across our method and all baselines.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Baseline Implementations</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System-level Baselines.VideoRAG-A</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite> is a retrieval method that encodes each video segment by linearly interpolating its textual and visual representations. We set <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> as 0.5 in this set up. <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GQR</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib81" title="" class="ltx_ref">59</a>]</cite> refines the retriever’s query embedding by gradient descent against a mixture of the two retriever’s score distributions, using KL minimization. We set two retrievers as text and video retrievers with learning rate <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\mathrm{e}{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\mathrm{e}{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FreeRet</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib83" title="" class="ltx_ref">89</a>]</cite> repurposes an MLLM (Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite> in our setup) as a training-free two-stage retriever, extracting segment embeddings from the last self-attention sublayer and reranking the candidates via MCQ-based scoring. <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GME</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib84" title="" class="ltx_ref">85</a>]</cite> is a unified multimodal embedding model based on Qwen2-VL-2B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib86" title="" class="ltx_ref">61</a>]</cite>. We apply both methods directly to the raw video segments and query.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Query-level Baselines.VideoRAG-B</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">42</a>]</cite> prompts Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> to decouple each query into three memory-specific sub-queries, retrieves from each memory, and merges the results before passing them to the generator. Following the original paper, we use one visual retriever and two text retrievers. <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RRF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib82" title="" class="ltx_ref">50</a>]</cite> is the RAG-Fusion variant of reciprocal rank fusion: the MLLM (Qwen3-VL-8B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>) rewrites each query into two modality-targeted paraphrases — one for text-clip, one for text-frames — which drive two retrievers operating on the text-clip and text-frame embeddings, respectively. The resulting ranked lists are aggregated by the standard RRF formula with <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k{=}60" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k{=}60</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DAT</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib55" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> adaptively balances two retrievers per query using LLM. We set the paper’s dense and sparse setting with text clip and frames, <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> that interpolates the min-max-normalized similarities over the candidate union. <span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">UniversalRAG</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>]</cite> routes each query to a single optimal <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,g)</annotation></semantics></math> configuration using a trained classifier and applies the selected configuration uniformly to all retrieved chunks. We implement two variants-an LLM-based router (Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct fine-tuned with LoRA <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r{=}32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r{=}32</annotation></semantics></math>, BCE multi-hot supervision) and a lightweight encoder-based router (T5Gemma 2 270M <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib87" title="" class="ltx_ref">80</a>]</cite> with a linear classification head) — and replace the paper’s sigmoid-thresholded decoding with argmax at inference for consistency with the top-<math id="A4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> retrieval setting used by all other baselines.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Router Implementations.</span>

To evaluate the benefits of chunk-level decisions, we compare <span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CARVE</span> against two types of query-level routers that select a single configuration <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m,g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m,g)</annotation></semantics></math> per query. To train LLM-based Router, following the training recipe of UniversalRAG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib80" title="" class="ltx_ref">76</a>]</cite>, we fine-tune Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> as a multi-label classifier over the four configurations. We apply LoRA (<math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=32</annotation></semantics></math>) and train for 5 epochs with a <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\mathrm{e}{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mathrm{e}{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> learning rate. Labels are derived from our train set, where a configuration is labeled positive if it produces a correct answer. At inference, we select the configuration with the highest predicted score (<span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">argmax</span>) and apply it uniformly to all chunks for both retrieval and generation. To train encoder based router, we train an MLP-based classifier on top of a frozen BGE-large-en-v1.5 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib85" title="" class="ltx_ref">68</a>]</cite> encoder. We use the frozen <span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">[CLS]</span> representation as input to a classification head consisting of three hidden blocks with a size of 512. The model is optimized using binary cross-entropy with a <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\mathrm{e}{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\mathrm{e}{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> learning rate. Similar to the LLM router, we use <span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">argmax</span> at inference to determine a single, query-uniform configuration.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Evaluation Metrics</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate retrieval and generation separately. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of evaluation queries. For each query <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathcal{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathcal{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of ground-truth evidence chunks annotated for <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{q}^{K}=[r_{1},r_{2},\ldots,r_{K}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{q}^{K}=[r_{1},r_{2},\ldots,r_{K}]</annotation></semantics></math> be the ranked list of the top-<math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> retrieved chunks. In our main experiments, we set <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Recall@K.</span>
Recall@K measures whether the ground-truth evidence appears in the top-<math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> retrieved chunks. For a query <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A4.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Recall@K}(q)=\frac{|R_{q}^{K}\cap G_{q}|}{|G_{q}|}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Recall</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>K</mi></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Recall@K}(q)=\frac{|R_{q}^{K}\cap G_{q}|}{|G_{q}|}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The dataset-level score is the average over all queries:</p>
<table id="A4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Recall@K}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{Recall@K}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Recall</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>Recall</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Recall@K}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{Recall@K}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Since each query in <span id="A4.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">V-RAGBench</span> is designed to have a uniquely sufficient evidence chunk, this reduces to checking whether that evidence chunk is retrieved within the top-<math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">nDCG@K.</span>
nDCG@K evaluates not only whether the evidence is retrieved, but also how highly it is ranked. We use binary relevance:</p>
<table id="A4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{rel}_{i}=\mathbbm{1}[r_{i}\in G_{q}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>rel</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{rel}_{i}=\mathbbm{1}[r_{i}\in G_{q}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the chunk ranked at position <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The discounted cumulative gain is</p>
<table id="A4.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{DCG@K}(q)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}\frac{\mathrm{rel}_{i}}{\log_{2}(i+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>DCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mfrac><msub><mi>rel</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{DCG@K}(q)=\sum_{i=1}^{K}\frac{\mathrm{rel}_{i}}{\log_{2}(i+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p">The ideal discounted cumulative gain is</p>
<table id="A4.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{IDCG@K}(q)=\sum_{i=1}^{\min(K,|G_{q}|)}\frac{1}{\log_{2}(i+1)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>IDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{IDCG@K}(q)=\sum_{i=1}^{\min(K,|G_{q}|)}\frac{1}{\log_{2}(i+1)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p">Then,</p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{nDCG@K}(q)=\frac{\mathrm{DCG@K}(q)}{\mathrm{IDCG@K}(q)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>nDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>DCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>IDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{nDCG@K}(q)=\frac{\mathrm{DCG@K}(q)}{\mathrm{IDCG@K}(q)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p">The final nDCG@K is averaged over all queries:</p>
<table id="A4.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{nDCG@K}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{nDCG@K}(q)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>nDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>nDCG</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{nDCG@K}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}\mathrm{nDCG@K}(q).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pass Rate.</span>
For generation, we report aggregate pass rate. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> be the model-generated answer for query <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> be the ground-truth answer. We use an LLM-as-a-judge <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to determine whether <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{a}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{a}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> is correct:</p>
<table id="A4.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(q,\hat{a}_{q},a_{q})\in\{0,1\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(q,\hat{a}_{q},a_{q})\in\{0,1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that the generated answer matches the key factual content of the reference answer. The pass rate is</p>
<table id="A4.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{PassRate}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}J(q,\hat{a}_{q},a_{q})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>PassRate</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{PassRate}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}J(q,\hat{a}_{q},a_{q}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Latency.</span>
We additionally report latency for experiments where methods differ in online inference cost. For each query <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the wall-clock time required by the evaluated online pipeline. Depending on the experiment, this includes query encoding, retrieval, reranking, evidence rendering, and generation, but excludes offline preprocessing such as video chunking, memory construction and index construction. The average latency is</p>
<table id="A4.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Latency}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}T_{q}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Latency</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒬</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Latency}=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{Q}|}\sum_{q\in\mathcal{Q}}T_{q}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">When reporting retrieval-only latency, <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> includes only the online retrieval and reranking steps; when reporting end-to-end latency, it additionally includes generation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>LLM-as-a-Judge Details</h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For evaluating answer correctness on open-ended questions, we use Qwen3.6-35B-A3B as the backbone model for the LLM-as-a-judge. The prompt used for judgment is shown in Figure <a href="#A7.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ G.3 LLM Judge Prompt ‣ Appendix G Prompts ‣ Rethinking RAG in Long Videos: What to Retrieve and How to Use It?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Human Verification.</span> To assess the reliability of the LLM-as-a-judge, we conduct human validation of its outputs. We randomly sample <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="600" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>600</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">600</annotation></semantics></math> instances from the full set of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}100</annotation></semantics></math> predictions (corresponding to a <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="95\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>95</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">95\%</annotation></semantics></math> confidence interval with a margin of error of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 4</annotation></semantics></math>). We apply the same annotator qualification criteria as in Section <a href="#A3.SS5" title="C.5 QA Filter Details ‣ Appendix C Dataset ‣ Rethinking RAG in Long Videos: What to Retrieve and How to Use It?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a>, namely (i) graduate students in the field of AI, (ii) at least one first-author publication at a top-tier AI conference, (iii) English proficiency equivalent to CEFR C2, and (iv) completion of a 30-minute instructional briefing prior to annotation. Each annotator is then provided with the model-generated answer, the ground-truth answer, and the binary decision from the LLM-as-a-judge indicating whether the prediction is correct, and is asked to independently assess whether the binary judge’s evaluation label should be considered correct.
We find substantial agreement between human annotators and the LLM-as-a-judge, with a Cohen’s Kappa score of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.61" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.61</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.61</annotation></semantics></math>. Further inspection shows that in <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.2\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the instances, both annotators agree that the LLM-as-a-judge made an incorrect decision. These results suggest that while assessing open-ended questions with a binary LLM-as-a-judge may introduce minor noise, it can be considered generally reliable for large-scale evaluation.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span><span id="A5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CARVE</span> Algorithm</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ Appendix E CARVE Algorithm ‣ Rethinking RAG in Long Videos: What to Retrieve and How to Use It?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> shows the formalization of the algorithm of <span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CARVE</span>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CARVE</span>: Chunk-Aware Reranking for Video Evidence</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
            
            
             Per-wearer video corpus <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> (2-min non-overlapping chunks)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
            
            
             Query <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
            
            
             Multimodal encoder <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> (Qwen3-VL-Embedding-2B by default)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
            
            
             Multimodal cross-encoder <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{CE}(\cdot,\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>CE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{CE}(\cdot,\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> (Qwen3-VL-Reranker-2B by default)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
            
            
             Captioner MLLM (Qwen3-VL-8B) for textual summaries (cap <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math> tokens)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
            
            
             Keyframe count <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> (default <math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>)

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
            
            
             Per-configuration retrieval cap <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, final list size <math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
            
            
             Generator <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
            
            
             Multi-representation index <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
            
            
             Tagged final top-<math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> list <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{q}^{\star}=\{(v,\,(m^{\star}_{v},g^{\star}_{v}))\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>m</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>v</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{q}^{\star}=\{(v,\,(m^{\star}_{v},g^{\star}_{v}))\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
            
            
             Predicted answer <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{a}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
            
            
          
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
            
            
          <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:345.0pt;height:0.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Offline: Chunk-wise Multi-Representation Indexing</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
            
            
          <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:345.0pt;height:0.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
            
            
          <span id="alg1.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each chunk <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒱</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{V}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
            
            
            <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{K}(v)\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{K}(v)\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> keyframes from <math id="alg1.l19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-means++ <em id="alg1.l19.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">centroids</em> over per-frame embeddings of <math id="alg1.l19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
            
            
